          "description": "We are looking for a Full Stack Engineer to join our dynamic team.\nWe build scalable web applications using React/NodeJS/PostgreSQL. Our core technologies are Next.js and Supabase.\nThe ideal candidate has a strong foundation of backend logic & databases and has production experience.\nYou will be working directly with clients abroad on exciting cutting edge products.\nWho we are\nAZKY Tech Labs is a UK/Dubai based agency that specializes in building AI powered solutions (SaaS, Internal tools etc) for clients around the world. Over the past 5 years, we have worked with more than 100 foreign companies (startups, SMEs and Enterprises) in USA, UK, EU and Australia.\nWho You Are\nYou're a good fit if you have strong foundations and production experience in React/Node/PostgreSQL.\nAvailability : This role is for immediate hiring. It is not suitable for candidates who are currently employed full-time in another role.\nPrimary Interest : You have a strong, demonstrable passion for backend development. Your primary interest must be in server-side logic, APIs, and databases, not just UI development.\nTechnical Foundation : You must have solid experience with React.js, Node.js (ideally building REST APIs, e.g., with Express), Relational Databases (e.g., PostgreSQL or MySQL). You have architected databases from scratch.\nCore Concepts : You have a strong grasp of Data Structures, Algorithms, and Client-Server Architecture.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain web and mobile applications\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code following industry best practices.\nCollaborate with QA, and product teams to deliver robust features.\nOptimize application performance, scalability, and security.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the stack.\nParticipate in code reviews, provide feedback, and ensure code quality.\nStay updated with emerging technologies and frameworks to enhance development efficiency.\nSoft skills\nGood English\nStrong attention to detail\nProactive, independent working style\nStrong communication and teamwork skills\nEffective time management and ability to prioritize tasks\nDesire to learn and grow as a developer\nSalary Range: Competitive\nPerks for you\nQuarterly Performance Bonus- based on performance and client outcomes\nCompany equipment (up to PKR 130k allowance to upgrade workstation)\nLaptop allowance (when you use your own laptop)\nInternet backup\nMedical insurance (dependents and parents included)\nDirect communication with clients and PMs (US, UK, EU) on a regular basis\nPaid time off\nFully remote and open work culture",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485058457": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:45:00.718326+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nWe are seeking a technically strong Distributed Cache & Java Support Engineer to support distributed caching solutions and onboard Java and Spring Boot application use cases to the distributed-cache platform.\nThe candidate will combine hands-on Java development with practical enterprise distributed cache or in-memory data grid experience.\nThe role focuses on cache use-case assessment and onboarding, Java integration support, distributed-cache troubleshooting, and JVM diagnostics.\nKey Responsibilities\nProvide production support for distributed cache clusters and related Java application integrations\nMonitor cluster health, partition distribution, memory, latency, throughput, capacity, and performance\nSupport cache configuration and troubleshooting across distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction and expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup and replication, serialization, and cluster discovery\nDiagnose cache-related incidents including high latency, memory pressure, member restarts, split-brain conditions, data inconsistency, and degraded performance\nCoordinate with application, infrastructure, and vendor support teams to investigate issues and drive technical resolution\nReview and modify Java or Spring Boot code required to onboard application use cases to the distributed-cache platform\nWork with application teams to understand the use case, data model, access pattern, expected load, and caching objectives\nImplement application-side cache integration changes and validate serialization, distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/TTL, and client configuration\nTroubleshoot JVM and application issues encountered during onboarding, integration testing, and production stabilization\nMinimum Qualification & Experience\nBachelor's degree in computer science, Software Engineering, or Information Technology\n7+ years of relevant experience in Java backend development, Java application support, distributed systems, or closely related engineering work\n3+ years of hands-on experience with distributed caching or in-memory data grid technologies in conjunction with Java applications\nMust Have\nStrong hands-on Java development experience, including the ability to write and modify Java code\nStrong JVM troubleshooting capability, including memory management, garbage collection, thread dumps, heap analysis, and performance diagnosis\nHands-on Spring Boot development or application-support experience, including cache integration or use-case onboarding\nHands-on experience with any distributed caching or in-memory data grid technology such as Redis, Hazelcast, Apache Ignite, Ehcache, Oracle Coherence, Infinispan, Memcached, or comparable platforms. Training will be provided on the selected platform.\nStrong understanding of distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup/replication, split-brain, serialization, and cluster discovery\nGood to Have\nProduction application support experience in banking, telecom, or other mission-critical environments, including incident triage, root cause analysis, and documentation\nBasic support-level exposure to Kubernetes, containers, Linux, networking, and optionally Anthos or OpenShift; deep platform expertise is not required\nFamiliarity with CI/CD processes and deployment-pipeline troubleshooting\nExperience with Splunk, AppDynamics, or Hazel cast Management Center, plus basic TLS/mTLS and certificate troubleshooting.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
