          "description": "About the Company\nUSAble Life is hiring Developer I/II professionals to support the development and maintenance of its software applications and company systems.\nAbout the Role\nThe Developer I/II will analyze, develop, implement, maintain, and test software applications across the company's systems. The position is suited to candidates with a computer science or information systems degree and at least one year of IT experience.\nKey Responsibilities\nAnalyze software application requirements and system needs\nDevelop and implement software applications across company systems\nMaintain existing applications and support ongoing system functionality\nTest applications to help ensure they perform as expected\nRequired Qualifications\nDegree in Computer Science (CS) or Information Systems (IS)\nAt least one year of IT experience\nPreferred Skills\nKnowledge of Git\nSQL skills\nLocation and Work Arrangement\nRemote opportunities available\nEquipment provided\nCompensation and Benefits\nPerformance-based incentive plan\nUSAble Life provides pay ranges for Web Developer I and Web Developer II, including base compensation and potential bonuses.",
