        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:45:00.718326+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486521172": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:45:00.718326+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Role Description The Full Stack Developer (.NET + React) will design, develop, and maintain Power App applications.\nQualifications\nCandidates should possess strong Full-Stack Development and Software Development skills, with hands-on experience in .NET and React.\nCandidates should possess solid Back-End Web Development skills, including API design, data access layers, and integration with databases.\nExposure to MS Power Platform specifically Power Apps is a key requirement.\nCandidates should possess Front-End Development skills, including React, Cascading Style Sheets (CSS), and responsive, accessible UI implementation.\nCandidates should possess familiarity with modern development practices such as version control (e.g., Git), unit testing, and continuous integration.\nCandidates should possess problem-solving abilities, attention to detail, and the capacity to work collaboratively in a hybrid environment.\nRelevant qualifications may include a degree or diploma in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\nExperience with cloud platforms, microservices, or data visualization is beneficial, as is prior work on simulation or modeling solutions.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-04T23:45:00.718326+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://pe.linkedin.com/posts/khursheed-jahan-ara-8baa93110_koderlabs-is-hiring-for-associate-software-activity-7185587254185082880-4FE0": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "KoderLabs is hiring for Associate Software Engineer - Node JS.\n\nLocation: Karachi (Onsite)\nRequirement: Enrolled in final semester of BSCS or Software Engineering. Prior relevant internship experience is a plus.\n\nApply away at jobs@koderlabs.com and mention \"ASE-NodeJS\" in subject line.",
          "posted_at": "2024-04-15T10:38:23.128Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ahad-khan-hrmanager_were-hiring-nodejs-developer-12-years-activity-7462111595511312384-LkQT": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "🚀 We're Hiring: Node.js Developer (1–2 Years Exp.)\nCompany: Bitrupt\nLocation: Saddar, Karachi (Near Press Club) – On-site\n\nThe Role\nWe aren't looking for a corporate robot. We need a rising backend builder who lives in Node.js, breathes APIs, and is ready to write code that actually impacts real products. If you have 1 to 2 years of solid experience and love solving puzzles behind the screen, let’s talk.\n\nWhat You’ll Bring to the Table\nNode.js Mastery: You know your way around Express.js (or NestJS) and event-driven architecture.\nDatabase Comfort: You can talk to MongoDB or SQL databases without breaking a sweat.\nAPI Crafting: You build clean, secure, and fast RESTful APIs.\nProblem-Solving: You don't just find bugs; you crush them.\n\nWhy Bitrupt?\nWork right in the heart of Karachi (Saddar), easily accessible from anywhere.\nFast-paced environment with zero corporate red tape.\nMassive room for quick professional and financial growth.\n\nDrop Your Specs!\n📧 Email: Send your resume to careers@bitrupt.co\n👉 Use Subject: Node.js Developer - [Your Name]\n📞 WhatsApp / Call: 0303-2518858",
          "posted_at": "2026-05-18T12:07:23.677Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aqsajavedofficial_we-are-hiring-for-a-senior-nodejs-backend-activity-7429784005496967168-lZt8": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "We are hiring for a Senior Node.js Backend Developer with 5–8 years of experience to join our team in Karachi on-site.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n- Design and develop scalable backend services using Node.js\n- Build secure RESTful APIs and microservices\n- Optimize performance, reliability, and system architecture\n- Collaborate with product, frontend, and DevOps teams\n- Ensure code quality, security, and best development practices\n\nRequirements:\n- 5–8 years of backend development experience\n- Strong expertise in Node.js and JavaScript/TypeScript\n- Experience with databases (MongoDB/MySQL/PostgreSQL)\n- Solid understanding of system design, APIs, and security standards\n- Experience in fintech/payments is a strong plus\n\nInterested candidates can apply by sending their resumes to aqsa.javed@kamelpay.com.",
          "posted_at": "2026-02-18T07:09:05.603Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/heykristopher_xbox-is-building-a-new-kind-of-flywheel-with-ugcPost-7513955395246161920-7a3g": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "XBOX is building a new kind of flywheel with games at the center.\n\nThe company announced XP this morning (a clever title)—a new division headed by Kayleen Walters focused on creating more on-ramps for fans to its beloved IP through film & television, consumer products, live events, and strategic partnerships.\n\nHere are the four divisions:\n\n* XBOX PICTURES: Bringing our worlds and characters to new audiences through film, television, and other forms of linear storytelling. \n* XBOX PRODUCTS: Creating products that are authentic to the fandom that allow fans to celebrate and express the franchises they love. \n* XBOX PLACES: Bringing communities together through live events, immersive experiences, attractions, broadcasts, and destinations. \n* XBOX PARTNERSHIPS: Working with creators, brands, and communities to develop new experiences, sponsorships, and brand partnerships.\n\nThe move—championed by Matthew Ball following an internal memo from Asha Sharma—is both elegant and strategic. It adopts the best strategies from Disney and Nintendo, both of whom understand that content is king. Where Disney’s flywheel was built strategically around film and television firs, Nintendo’s is game first.\n\nWith this move, XBOX is positioning itself to move beyond being a mere platform to owning its market position as both a publisher and steward of massive IP (from Minecraft to Halo and beyond).\n\nI’m excited to see where this leads.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-08T13:36:09.005Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hira-wahid-437ab0267_we-are-hiring-position-nodejs-developer-activity-7464631549171347458-EXue": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "🚀 We are Hiring!!!!\n\nPosition: Node.js Developer\nExperience: Fresh – 1 Year\n\n📍 Location: DHA Phase 2 Ext, Karachi.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDevelop and maintain backend applications using Node.js\nBuild and integrate REST APIs\nDebug and troubleshoot application issues\nCollaborate with development teams\nWork with databases and third-party integrations\n\nRequirements:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field\nGood understanding of JavaScript and Node.js\nFamiliarity with Express.js and REST APIs\nBasic knowledge of MongoDB/MySQL\nUnderstanding of Git/version control is a plus\nGood problem-solving and communication skills\n\n📩 Interested candidates can share their resumes at hira.wahid@cee-solutions.com or hr@resourcelinked.tech with the position mentioned in the subject line",
          "posted_at": "2026-05-25T11:00:47.451Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/pakistan-it-jobs_hiring-backend-developer-nodejs-karachi-activity-7389224553194881024-m6qX": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Hiring: Backend Developer (Node.js) – Karachi, Onsite\nWe’re looking for a passionate Backend Developer with strong expertise in Node.js to join our growing tech team in Karachi.\n\nWhat We’re Looking For:\n2+ years of hands-on experience with Node.js & Express.js\nStrong understanding of APIs, RESTful services & database design (MongoDB/MySQL)\nExperience with version control (Git)\nProblem-solving mindset & teamwork attitude\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\nBuild and maintain scalable backend systems\nCollaborate with frontend and mobile teams\nOptimize APIs for performance and security\n\n📍 Location: Karachi (Onsite)\n 🕒 Job Type: Full-time\nsend your cv at : hr@asoratech.com",
          "posted_at": "2025-10-29T09:00:18.607Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/rohail-zafar-857558225_hiring-fullstackdeveloper-nodejs-activity-7523367745237803008-V33e": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "We’re Hiring: Full Stack Developer\n\nAce On Technology is looking for a Full Stack Developer with 1.5–3 years of professional experience to join our growing team!\n\n Location: Gulistan-e-Johar, Karachi — Onsite\n Working Days: Monday to Saturday\n Employment Type: Full-time\n Experience Required: 1.5–3 Years\n\nRequired Skills:\nStrong hands-on experience with Node.js and Express.js\nProficiency in React.js\nGood understanding of JavaScript and TypeScript\nExperience working with MongoDB\nExperience with Browser/Chrome Extensions will be a strong plus.\n\n Please Note: This is an onsite position in Karachi. We encourage applications only from candidates who are currently residing in Karachi or are willing to relocate to Karachi.\n\n Before applying, please read the complete Job Description carefully and ensure your skills and experience align with the requirements.\n\n How to Apply:\n\nInterested candidates can DM me directly or send their CV to \nhr@aceontechnology.com\n\nPlease mention the following along with your CV:\n\n Current Salary\n Expected Salary\n Notice Period\n\nIf you know someone who would be a good fit, feel free to tag them or share this post.\n\n#Hiring #FullStackDeveloper #NodeJS #ReactJS #TypeScript #MongoDB #KarachiJobs #TechJobs #PakistanJobs #OnsiteJobs #SoftwareJobs #aceontechnology",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-03T12:57:27.876Z"
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-04T23:47:44.488845+00:00"
  },
